{"name":"Sky City","hex":"#a0bdd9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"}],"entries":[{"title":"DJI Sky City","blocks":[{"text":"DJI Sky City is a two-tower office complex in Nanshan, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China. It is owned by DJI and serves as its global corporate headquarters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJI_Sky_City"},{"title":"FEDS Zhubei","blocks":[{"text":"FEDS Zhubei is a shopping mall located in Zhubei City, Hsinchu County, Taiwan that opened on 14 January 2022. With a total floor area of 141,117 m2 (1,518,970 sq ft), it is the largest shopping mall in Hsinchu County and is located near Hsinchu HSR station. This is the 13th store of the Far Eastern Department Stores company."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/FEDS_Zhubei_20220227.jpg/330px-FEDS_Zhubei_20220227.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FEDS_Zhubei"},{"title":"Sky City (Changsha)","blocks":[{"text":"Sky City, or Sky City One, was an 838-metre-tall (2,749 ft) planned skyscraper in the city of Changsha, Hunan in south-central China. The prospective builders, Broad Sustainable Building, estimated it would take just 90 days to construct. Including the 120 days needed for prefabrication before on-site work commenced, the total time needed was 210 days. Pre-construction activities were halted in August 2013 after government regulators required additional approvals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/J220_Sky_City_Changsha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_City_(Changsha)"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg/120px-FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg/250px-FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg/120px-FEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling_1F.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFEDS_Zhubei_Hakka_Ceiling